-- Cloze answers: accept the reading of what is written in the blank.
--
-- A cloze accepted the surface, the dictionary form and the DICTIONARY FORM's
-- reading, but not the reading of the text actually in the blank. A sentence
-- writing ６つ therefore rejected むっつ — the correct reading of what is on
-- screen — and the reader was told they were wrong for being right.
--
-- CONTENT ONLY. This touches `exercise_prompts.answer` and nothing else: no
-- accounts, no srs_cards, no review logs. Safe to run on a live database, and
-- safe to run twice.
--
-- Apply on the server (no pnpm or npm needed):
--   docker cp cloze-answers.sql dmb-postgres:/tmp/cloze-answers.sql
--   docker exec -i dmb-postgres sh -c \
--     'psql -U "$POSTGRES_USER" -d nihongo -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -f /tmp/cloze-answers.sql'
--   docker exec -i dmb-postgres rm /tmp/cloze-answers.sql
BEGIN;
